# Overrides only. The IDE merges this file with its bundled defaults
# (since 2020.2) -- see the reference block at the bottom. Edit via
# Help | Edit Custom VM Options.
#
# NOTE: This file tunes the JVM FRONTEND only. The ReSharper backend
# (Rider.Backend.exe) is a separate .NET process with its own memory
# profile; raising -Xmx above ~6g gives almost no benefit and steals
# RAM from MSBuild / Roslyn / Docker.
-Xms3g
-Xmx6g
# Compact object headers (JEP 519, a product flag since JDK 25): smaller
# objects, so a lower live heap. Rider 2026.1 runs on JBR 25 but only
# turns this on by default from 2026.2; drop this line once on 2026.2+.
-XX:+UseCompactObjectHeaders

# --- 2026.1 platform defaults on JBR 25 (commented reference; do not uncomment) ---
# Listed here so drift is visible if JetBrains changes a default in a
# future release. If any of these ever needs a non-default value, move
# that single line above this block. Products may append a few lines of
# their own. G1 is the JVM's own default collector and UTF-8 the default
# file encoding (JEP 400), so neither needs a line.
#
# -Xms / -Xmx                                  (product-specific; overridden above)
# -XX:JbrShrinkingGcMaxHeapFreeRatio=40         (idle heap shrinking)
# -XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=512m                (JIT code cache)
# -XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError               (diagnostics)
# -XX:-OmitStackTraceInFastThrow                (full stacks)
# -XX:CICompilerCount=2                         (JIT threads)
# -XX:+IgnoreUnrecognizedVMOptions              (survives stale user flags)
# -XX:+UnlockDiagnosticVMOptions
# -XX:TieredOldPercentage=100000
# -ea                                           (assertions)
# -Dsun.io.useCanonCaches=false
# -Dsun.java2d.metal=true                       (macOS rendering)
# -Djbr.catch.SIGABRT=true
# -Djdk.http.auth.tunneling.disabledSchemes=""
# -Djdk.attach.allowAttachSelf=true
# -Djdk.module.illegalAccess.silent=true
# -Djdk.nio.maxCachedBufferSize=2097152
# -Djava.util.zip.use.nio.for.zip.file.access=true
# -Dkotlinx.coroutines.debug=off
# -Dskiko.rendering.useScreenMenuBar=false
#
# Added in 2026.2: -XX:+UseCompactObjectHeaders and
# --sun-misc-unsafe-memory-access=allow
